# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored.
#
# ⚠ ONLY Supabase's URL and ANON key belong here.
#
# Anything prefixed VITE_ is inlined into the built JavaScript and is therefore
# PUBLIC — readable by anyone who opens devtools on the deployed site. The anon
# key is designed for that; Row Level Security is the real boundary.
#
# NEVER put these in a VITE_ variable:
#   - the Supabase service-role key (bypasses RLS entirely — total data exposure)
#   - Twelve Data / Finnhub / Marketaux / metals.dev keys
#   - Gemini or Mistral API keys
#   - the Telegram bot token
#   - the Web Push VAPID private key
#   - the Brevo API key
#
# Those all live in Supabase Edge Function secrets and are only ever used
# server-side:
#   supabase secrets set FINNHUB_API_KEY=...
#
# The repo is public (a GitHub Pages requirement on the free plan), so a secret
# committed here is a secret published.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Supabase → Project Settings → API
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# Optional. Defaults to /gettingrich/ — must match the GitHub repo name, or every
# asset 404s on the deployed site. CI sets this automatically from the repo name.
# VITE_BASE=/gettingrich/
